      "claim": "L1 human absolute-bioavailability records for ester-containing or basic-amine drugs are above the 20% threshold: benazepril 28–37% (C01, C16), pivampicillin 50–89% (C03, C13, C21), tamoxifen approximately 100% (C02, C04, C05), norethisterone 47–73% (C11), and encainide 76–78% in cirrhosis (C08, C12, C19). This indicates that the query's acetate ester and tertiary amine do not by themselves support F < 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C01","C16","C03","C13","C21","C02","C04","C05","C11","C08","C12","C19"]
