  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct diltiazem-specific absolute oral bioavailability record is supplied.",
    "No modified-release formulation-matched F or matched oral-versus-IV exposure comparison is available for the query.",
    "L5 gut-wall efflux/intestinal-metabolism records are mechanistic and mostly for other molecules; they do not directly quantify the query's first-pass loss.",
    "The query's ester hydrolysis and CYP3A4-related first-pass metabolism are not directly measured in the supplied records.",
    "Silymarin nanoemulsion (C68, C70) and pemafibrate pH-gradient (C71) records are formulation- or compound-specific and have low transferability to the query."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F >= 20%) because L1 human F records for ester-containing and basic-amine drugs, L4 high-absorption/high-permeability evidence for similar basic amines, and L5 gut-wall efflux records showing high permeability without an affirmative efflux barrier all support adequate absorption; no transferable affirmative low-F evidence is present, and the modified-release condition does not by itself imply F < 20%. Confidence remains moderate because no direct diltiazem F record is supplied."
}

